 "kit": "A Flamebrand, a sacred warrior of the fire god: heavy blackened iron plate over scale with rusted edges on the arms and legs, worn under a sleeveless surcoat of dull ember-orange cloth that covers his whole chest and belly from the collar down to just below the knees, front and back, split at the front below the belt so the legs can stride and held at the waist by a black iron-studded belt; a tall closed dark iron helm topped by a crest of iron flames and a dull ember-orange plume; a long cape of the same ember-orange cloth from the shoulders to the backs of the knees; a straight longsword whose blade is wreathed in real flame, the only bright light on the figure. No shield, no horns. Taller and prouder than a warrior.",
